    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2026/01/hoka-cielo-x1-30-review-2026.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The very high-stack dual-layer PEBA midsole is soft and highly impact-protective, especially in the heel/midfoot; heel landings compress and smooth out impact, while the forefoot feels more rockered/plate-driven and better for rolling than landing.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is a major strength with a very bouncy ride and snappy forefoot transition, making it feel fast over tempo-to-marathon efforts, though it is less sharp for very short all-out intervals.",
        "Stability: This is a neutral setup with mild guidance, but the narrow heel/midfoot platform plus soft foam can feel wobbly laterally; heel lockdown is secure with a small flexible heel counter, so it favors runners with stable mechanics.",
        "Durability: Outsole rubber strips showed no noticeable wear after about 30 hard miles and traction remained strong, but exposed midsole showed slight wear; expected durability is moderate/average for a super shoe with some risk of posterolateral piece damage for heavy strikers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2026/01/hoka-cielo-x-1-30-review-all-good.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The PEBA midsole is very soft and bouncy, and the high, almost luxuriously cushioned heel improves impact protection while feeling best for forefoot/midfoot runners.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is a standout, with a lively bounce and a more accessible MetaRocker that makes turnover feel quick and efficient.",
        "Stability: Compared with v2, stability is clearly improved via the redesigned heel section, removal of midsole cutouts, stout upper structure, and a tall padded heel counter with strong lockdown; heel strikers may still prefer the more stable Rocket X 3.",
        "Durability: Longevity looks strong from the lighter but more durable Leno-woven upper plus generous outsole rubber and tread coverage in key wear areas."
      ]
    }
  ],
